{"id":"letter-combinations-of-a-phone-number","title":"Letter Combinations of a Phone Number","difficulty":"Medium","pattern":"Backtracking","tags":["String","Backtracking","Hash Table"],"companies":{"google":3,"apple":2,"meta":3,"amazon":4,"microsoft":3},"description":"On a classic phone keypad each digit from 2 to 9 maps to letters: 2 -> abc, 3 -> def, 4 -> ghi, 5 -> jkl, 6 -> mno, 7 -> pqrs, 8 -> tuv, 9 -> wxyz.\n\nGiven a string `digits` containing only characters `2`-`9`, return every string that can be typed by picking one letter for each digit, in order. If `digits` is empty return an empty list. The results may be in any order.","examples":[{"input":"digits = \"23\"","output":"[\"ad\",\"ae\",\"af\",\"bd\",\"be\",\"bf\",\"cd\",\"ce\",\"cf\"]","explanation":"3 choices for '2' times 3 choices for '3'."},{"input":"digits = \"\"","output":"[]"},{"input":"digits = \"2\"","output":"[\"a\",\"b\",\"c\"]"}],"constraints":["0 <= digits.length <= 7","digits[i] is one of '2'..'9'"],"hints":["This is a Cartesian product: one letter per digit, independent choices.","Recurse over the digit index; for each letter of the current digit, append it and recurse on the next digit. Record when the index reaches len(digits).","Remember the empty-input special case: no digits means no combinations, not one empty string."],"function":"letterCombinations","signature":"def letterCombinations(self, digits: str) -> List[str]:","arg_types":{"digits":"str"},"return_type":"List[str]","compare":"unordered","tests":[{"input":{"digits":"23"},"output":["ad","ae","af","bd","be","bf","cd","ce","cf"]},{"input":{"digits":""},"output":[]},{"input":{"digits":"2"},"output":["a","b","c"]},{"input":{"digits":"79"},"output":["pw","px","py","pz","qw","qx","qy","qz","rw","rx","ry","rz","sw","sx","sy","sz"]},{"input":{"digits":"99"},"output":["ww","wx","wy","wz","xw","xx","xy","xz","yw","yx","yy","yz","zw","zx","zy","zz"]},{"input":{"digits":"2345679"},"output":["adgjmpw","adgjmpx","adgjmpy","adgjmpz","adgjm